tools.description:
Search the Spacefast API. Find operations and read their exact input and output types before you call them with execute. Results depend on the signed-in account's enabled features; calls still need the account's permissions.

Available in your code:
declare const tools: {
  search(options: { query: string; limit?: number; offset?: number }): Promise<{
    items: { path: string; name: string; description?: string }[];
    total: number;
    hasMore: boolean;
    nextOffset: number | null;
  }>;
  describe: {
    tool(options: { path: string }): Promise<{
      path: string;
      description?: string;
      inputTypeScript?: string; // absent when the operation takes no input
      outputTypeScript: string;
      typeScriptDefinitions?: Record<string, string>;
      error?: { code: "tool_not_found"; message: string; suggestions?: string[] };
    }>;
  };
};

Your code must be an async arrow function that returns the result. It runs in a sandbox without network, file, or credential access. It cannot call operations and changes nothing.

Examples:

// Find an operation by its exact name or by its purpose
async () => (await tools.search({ query: "getSpace", limit: 5 })).items

// Read one operation's input and output types
async () => tools.describe.tool({ path: "spacefast.org.session.spaces.updateSpace" })

Execute JavaScript code that can read, create, update, or delete resources through the Spacefast API: Spaces, deployments, source files, domains and DNS, sharing and credentials, teams, selling, tracking tags, webhooks, API keys, and account settings. First use the 'search' tool to find the right operation path and its input type, then write code that calls tools[path](input).

Available in your code:
type Result<T = unknown> =
  | { ok: true; data: T } // JSON responses keep the payload in data.data and list pagination in data.pagination
  | { ok: false; error: { code: string; message: string; details?: { code?: string } } };

declare const tools: {
  // path from search, such as "spacefast.org.session.spaces.listSpaces"
  [path: string]: (input?: Record<string, unknown>) => Promise<Result>;
};

// Show an image or deliver a file link next to the returned value.
declare function emit(
  content: { type: "image"; data: string; mimeType: string } | { type: "resource_link"; uri: string; name: string },
): void;

Calls use the signed-in user's permissions. Some operations send email, such as invitations. Some changes pause for approval: follow the returned resumePrompt with resume_execution, and never decide for the user.

Your code must be an async arrow function that returns the result. It runs in a sandbox with no network or file access except these calls, and each step between calls stops after 30 seconds.

Example: list Spaces
async () => {
  const spaces = await tools["spacefast.org.session.spaces.listSpaces"]({ limit: 20 });
  if (!spaces.ok) return spaces;
  return spaces.data.data.map((space) => ({ id: space.id, title: space.title, url: space.liveUrl }));
}
